            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Naming</h3>
                </div>
                <p><strong>Bhadradri</strong> The name Bhadradri comes from the famous Bhadrachalam Temple, which is a major religious and cultural landmark in the region.<br><strong>Kothagudem:</strong> Kothagudem is a significant town in the district, known for its coal mining industry, and serves as the administrative headquarters.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Formation of the District</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Telangana Reorganization: Bhadradri Kothagudem district was officially formed on October 11, 2016, as part of the reorganization of districts in Telangana. t shares borders with Chhattisgarh,<br><strong>Parent District:</strong>Before its formation, the area that now constitutes Bhadradri Kothagudem was part of the Khammam district.</p>
                <p>BhadradriKothagudem District comprises of (2) Revenue Divisions i.e., Bhadrachalam and Kothagudem with (23) Mandals, (479) Gram Panchayats and (377) Revenue Villages.</p>
                </div>            
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Jurisdiction</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Bhadradri Kothagdem District is named after Bhadrachalamhas famous Sri SeethaRama temple located in Bhadrachalam.This District was newly formed on October 11 2016 during reorganization of Districts.   The district is having large area of forest and most of the population belongs to Tribal’s. Kothagudem is the administrative headquarters of the District.The District is spread over an area of 7,483 square kilometers.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Demography of the District</h3>
                </div>
                <p>According to 2011 census, the district has population of 12,13,987 of which Female 6,10,454 and Male 6,03,533.Population density of 197 person/sq.km. It has sex ratio of 1008 and literacy rate of 66.40%.People belonging to various communities live in harmony. Majority of the Population consists of Tribal’s in the District.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Socio Economic Cultural peculiarity of the district</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Entire district comes under Tribal Sub - plan. 4 out of 5 Assembly constituencies are reserved for ST. The Rural-Urban ratio is pegged at 70: 30</p>
                <br>
                <p>                                     The District is having Tribal population in large number. Koyas, Lambadas and Kodareddies are accommodated in the District.  Majority of Tribal’s are from Koyacommunity followed by Lambadas. Whereas Konda Reddies belongs to primitive tribal groups lives on the hillocks of some pockets of the district.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Administrative set up of the district</h3>
                </div>
                <p>BhadradriKothagudem District comprises of (2) Revenue Divisions i.e., Bhadrachalam and Kothagudem with (23) Mandals, (479) Gram Panchayats and (377) Revenue Villages.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Roads & Transport</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Bhadradri Kothagudem district head quarte is well concted through Bhadrachalam Road Railway station from South Central Railways (Secunderabad) and there are TSRTC and APSRTC Bus services from Kothagudem to all important towns and other neibhourDistrictsand States. District head quarter is located 280 Kms from Hyderabad via Khammam.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Education</h3>
                </div>
                <p>The University College of Engineering Kakatiya University formally known as the Kothagudem School of Mines(KSM) is first mining college in Telanagana State and Second in India</p>
            </div>
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Industries</h3>
                </div>
                <p> <b>Singareni Collieries:</b>Singareni Collieries Company Limited (SCCL) is a major public sector coal mining company in India, operating primarily in the Bhadradri Kothagudem district. Here’s an overview of SCCL’s operations in Kothagudem:</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Overview</b></p>
                <p><b>Name:</b>Singareni Collieries Company Limited (SCCL)</p>
                <p><b>Loaction:</b>Kothagudem town, Bhadradri Kothagudem district, Telangana, India.</p>
                <p><b>Type:</b>Public sector coal mining company.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Kothagudem Thermal Power Station (KTPS) Breif Overview</b></p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Overview</b></p>
                <p><b>Type:</b>Coal-based thermal power plant.</p>
                <p><b>Capacity:</b>Approximately 1,720 MW.</p>
                <p><b>Operator:</b>Telangana State Power Generation Corporation Limited (TSGENCO).</p>
                <p><b>Fuel:</b>Primarily coal, sourced from Singareni Collieries Company Limited (SCCL).</p>
                <p><b>Key Role:</b>Supplies electricity to Telangana and neighboring regions.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>ITC Paperboards & Packaging, Sarapaka</b></p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Overview</b></p>
                <p><b>Name:</b>ITC Paperboards & Packaging, Sarapaka</p>
                <p><b>Loaction:</b>Sarapaka village, Bhadradri Kothagudem district, Telangana, India.</p>
                <p><b>Type:</b>Paperboard manufacturing facility.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Function and Importance</b></p>            
                <br>
                <p><b>Purpose:</b>The plant produces high-quality paperboard used for various packaging applications, including consumer goods, pharmaceuticals, and industrial products.</p>
                <p><b>Role:</b>Contributes to ITC Limited's paperboards and packaging division, which serves both domestic and international markets.</p>                
                <br>
                <p><b>Heavy Water Plant, Aswapuram</b></p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Overview</b></p>
                <p><b>Name:</b>Heavy Water Plant, Aswapuram</p>
                <p><b>Loaction:</b>Aswapuram village, Bhadradri Kothagudem district, Telangana, India.</p>
                <p><b>Type:</b>Heavy water production facility.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Function and Importance</b></p>            
                <br>
                <p><b>Purpose:</b>The plant produces heavy water (deuterium oxide, D₂O), which is used as a moderator and coolant in nuclear reactors.</p>
                <p><b>Role in Nuclear Program:</b>It supports India's nuclear power and weapons programs by providing crucial material for reactors.</p>                
                <br>
                <p><b>Culture and Festivals</b></p>            
                <br>
                <p><b>Festivals:</b>The district celebrates various cultural and religious festivals with great enthusiasm, including Sri Rama Navami, which is particularly significant due to the Bhadrachalam Temple.</p>                
                <br>
                <p><b>Transportation</b></p>            
                <br>
                <p><b>Road:</b>The district is well-connected by road to major cities in Telangana and neighboring states.</p>
                <p><b>Rail:</b>Kothagudem has a railway station that connects it to major cities in the region.</p>                
                <br>
                <p><b>Geography and Climate</b></p>            
                <br>
                <p><b>Location:</b>Bhadradri Kothagudem is situated in the southeastern part of Telangana.</p>
                <p><b>Terrain:</b>The district features a mix of hilly regions and plains, with the Godavari River flowing through it.</p>
                <p><b>Climate:</b>The region experiences a tropical climate with hot summers, moderate winters, and significant rainfall during the monsoon season.</p>                
                <br>                
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Place of Interest</h3>
                </div>
                <p><b>Bhadrachalam</b>, a key town of pilgrimage importance is located in Kothagudem district. The temple town of Bhadrachalam is situated on the bank of Godavari River. The town shares its historical significance with Ramayana Era. The name Bhadrachalam is derived from the word Bhadragiri (The Mountain Abode of Bhadra, the child of Meru and Menaka). The famous temple at Bhadrachalam is home to the ArchaMurthys of Rama, Sita and Lakshmana and their idols are believed to be swayambhu i.e., self-manifested ones.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>The Kinnerasani project </b> or the Dam is a storage reservoir constructed on the Kinnerasani River in the Godavari Basin at Yanambail village of Palvoncha Mandal. Kinnerasani River is an important tributary of the river Godavari. The scenic beauty created by the landscape along the Kinnerasani River is a panoramic one abutted by lush green landscape. The Kinnerasani sanctuary, a part of the Dandakaranya Forests, is a haven of exotic wildlife and tourists enjoy their visit here by spotting several animals in their natural habitat.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Parnashala</b>, a popular tourist place, is a village in the Dummugudem Mandal. It is said to be the place where the evil-minded king Ravana abducted Goddess Sita. This place unfolds this part of the epic Ramayana by exhibiting the primary events with beautifully canvassed sculptures of Shri Ram, Sita, Laxmana, and Ravan.</p>

